QuestGuidance.Register("en",27,{
[833]="7005874A\n1\tTake inventory (total: 12)\tSupplies can be found at Zarkul-sulûn. You should take inventory of supplies for Náin the Slakeless.\n2\tReport back to Náin the Slakeless\tNáin the Slakeless can be found at Zarkul-sulûn. You should report back to Náin the Slakeless.\n",
[834]="70028FBF\n1\tCollect missing nails (total: 15)\tNails have been borrowed from Rhianu by the various peoples of Galtrev and can likely be found around the village. You should collect the missing nails and return them to Rhianu so that her work on the siege-engine can be finished.\n2\tReturn the missing nails to Rhianu\tRhianu can be found at the fourth worksite in Galtrev. You should bring her the nails you collected so that she can finish her day's work.\n",
[835]="70058461\n1\tThe note contains directions to a specific location. Asking the scouts around Annâk-khurfu about this bat may give you some much-needed context.\t\n2\tTalk to Rékkur\tAll of the scouts you talked to about the bat have mentioned Rékkur, a dwarf who may be interested in what you've found. He stands guard in front of Annâk-khurfu.\n3\tGo to the overlook\tThe note describes an overlook west of the path leading up to Zarkul-sulûn, a ruin west of Annâk-khurfu. Rékkur has suggested that you venture to that location to see what's there.\n4\tSearch the body\030Read the note\030Examine the footprints\tThe note has brought you to the body of a dwarf scout near Zarkul-sulûn. You should search the body and the immediate area for clues to what has transpired.\n5\tTalk to Rékkur\tYou have found a new note, as well as possible clues to this scout's death. Rékkur will want to hear about your discoveries back at Annâk-khurfu.\n",
[836]="7005A661\n1\tDefeat frenzied stone-claws (total: 8)\030Collect strange runes (total: 10)\tStrange runes and frenzied stone-claws can both be found in the north-western section of Máttugard. You should collect the strange runes and defeat the frenzied stone-claws that you encounter.\n2\tTalk to Varthmath at Zidir-nesad\tVarthmath can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset, in Máttugard. You should talk to Varthmath at Zidir-nesad.\n3\tGive the strange runes to Voina\tVoina can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset, in Máttugard. You should give the strange runes to Voina.\n4\tTalk to Voina\tVoina can be found at Zidir-nesad, The Steepset, in Máttugard. You should talk to Voina.\n",
[837]="700173D3\n1\tDeliver the missive to Ornras at Echad Mirobel\030Collect Strange Missive\tMake your way to the ruins at Echad Mirobel located in the south-western reaches of Eregion. The message you found speaks of Angmar's desire to scour the remaining ruins for any remnant of power or knowledge that can be used to further strengthen their forces in the North. It mentions that an Uruk named Gûrsh has been placed in charge of the expedition.\n",
[838]="70035766\n1\tSummon Cyneberg to your side\tCyneberg has given you a whistle to summon her. You should summon Cyneberg to your side.\n2\tThe best path can be found south-west of Grimnesberg's crest. Cyneberg can be summoned using the whistle should you become separated. You should head south-west with Cyneberg to begin your return to Forlaw, and speak with her when she is ready.\t\n3\tAnother pile of Orcs can be found north-west of the first in the eastern High Knolls. You should investigate the Orcs with Cyneberg.\t\n4\tAnother pile of Orcs can be found north of the first in the eastern High Knolls. You should investigate the Orcs with Cyneberg.\t\n5\tFind the Orc-corpses to the north\tAnother pile of Orcs can be found north of the first in the eastern High Knolls. You should investigate the Orcs with Cyneberg.\n6\tTalk to Cyneberg\tCyneberg kneels at a pile of slain Orcs in the northern High Knolls. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n",
[839]="7000A2A5\n1\tSpend time looking for boars in Evendim\tEvendim is a big place. There should be boars somewhere. Parr Chopley is convinced that there must be boars somewhere in Evendim and wants you to spend some time looking for one.\n2\tTalk to Parr Chopley at Ost Forod\tParr Chopley is in Ost Forod, the old watch-post in the hills of Tyrn Fornech. You have found no sign of any boars in Evendim and should report your sad discovery to Parr Chopley.\n",
[840]="70044AB7\n1\tTalk to Bingo east of the town-centre of Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh\tBingo wants to travel to Galtrev, in Pren Gwydh. He will meet you inside the city, east of the centre of town.\n2\tTalk to Humfrey Rumming in Galtrev, in Dunland\tHumfrey Rumming is to the east of the town-centre of Galtrev, in Dunland.\n3\tGo to the location described by Humfrey's riddle to find Theodore and Haley\tHumfrey Rumming gave you a riddle to solve. It should point to the destination for which Haley Meadowsweet and Theodore Gorse were making.\n4\tTalk to Haley Meadowsweet in Avardin\tHaley Meadowsweet is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.\n5\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin\tTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.\n6\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin... again\tTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.\n7\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin... again\tTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.\n8\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin... again\tTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.\n9\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in Avardin... again\tTheodore Gorse is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.\n10\tTalk to Haley Meadowsweet in Avardin\tHaley Meadowsweet is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.\n11\tTalk to Bingo in Avardin, in Dunland\tBingo is in the town of Avardin, in Dunland.\n",
[841]="70022761\n1\tCollect proof that you made it to the attic\030Collect proof that you made it to the basement\030Collect proof that you made it to the Creeping Wing\030Collect proof that you made it to the Cobwebbed Wing\tProof of your visit to every corner of the Haunted Burrow lies in each of the levels off the main floor. You should collect proof that you have visited the four main areas of the Haunted Burrow and return before the time runs out.\n2\tReturn to Poppy Cotton with proof of your expedition\tPoppy Cotton is outside the Haunted Burrow, by the Party Tree. You should quickly return to Poppy Cotton with the proof that you bravely and skilfully walked in her footsteps inside the Haunted Burrow.\n",
[842]="70044470\n1\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back. See where Bergil wishes to go first.\n2\tGo see the ranks of soldiers\tGo to see the ranks of soldiers before the City Gates. Bergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n3\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back. See where Bergil wishes to go next.\n4\tGo see the ranks of soldiers\tGo to see another rank of soldiers before the City Gates. Bergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n5\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back. See where Bergil wishes to go next.\n6\tGo see the other soldiers\tRanks of soldiers can be found near the City Gates. Take Bergil to see more ranks of soldiers.\n7\tTalk to Rossaran\tRossaran the Swan-knight stands near the rude soldiers, inside the main gates of Minas Tirith. A swan-knight took note of the soldiers who were rude to Bergil, and seems to want to speak with you.\n8\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back. See where Bergil wishes to go next.\n9\tEnter the City Stables\030Take some apples\tThe City Stables stand across from the gates. Bergil wishes to feed some apples the horses in the City Stables. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n10\tThe City Stables stand across from the gates. Bergil wishes to feed some apples the horses in the City Stables. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\t\n11\tThe horses have devoured the apples.\t\n12\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back. See where Bergil wishes to go next.\n13\tAsk Himnir for treats\tThe Foodmongers' Market lies in the northern stretch of the First Circle. Help Bergil find the foodmonger Himnir and ask for a treat for all the children. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n14\tTalk to Amonel\tThe Wrights' Market lies in the southern stretch of the First Circle. Bring the broken whisk to the tinker Amonel in the Wrights' Market, as Himnir asked. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n15\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back. See what Bergil wishes to while you wait for the tinker to mend the whisk.\n16\tTour the southern wall\030Look out from over the City Gates\030Tour the northern wall\030Tour the far northern wall\tThe city walls can be reached via stairs from several points throughout the First Circle of Minas Tirith. Stroll with Bergil up upon the outer walls of Minas Tirith. If you should get separated, the whistle Bergil gave you will call him back.\n17\tTalk to Oryat\tWhile touring the city walls with Bergil, you have crossed paths with Oryat, the soldier who berated Bergil earlier. You should intervene before he lays his hands on the boy.\n18\tTalk to Bergil\tYou intervened to keep Oryat from striking Bergil, and Oryat challenged you to what is surely an ill-advised duel. See where Bergil wishes to go now. If you should get separated, the whistle Bergil gave you will call him back.\n19\tReturn to Amonel the tinker\tAmonel is in the Wrights' Fellow-hall, in the southern stretch of the First Circle. Return to the tinker Amonel, to see if Himnir's whisk has been mended. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n20\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back. See where Bergil wishes to go next.\n21\tMeet Oryat\tOryat will be waiting in the Second Circle, between the Feasting Hall and the tavern. Bergil has implored you to go and fight Oryat, to teach him a lesson. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n22\tDefeat Oryat\tOryat stands in the Second Circle, between the Feasting Hall and the tavern. Bergil has implored you to go and fight Oryat, to teach him a lesson. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n23\tTalk to Rossaran\tRossaran stands in the Second Circle, across from the Feasting Hall. After facing down the bully Oryat, you noticed the Swan-knight Rossaran standing nearby. See what he has to say. If you should get separated from Bergil, the whistle he gave you will call him back.\n24\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil will accompany you on the stroll. If you should get separated, the whistle he gave you will call him back. See what Bergil has to say.\n25\tMeet Bergil back at the Old Guest-house\tThe Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. You have beaten Oryat and scared him from troubling the children in the First Circle... but he has threatened harm to any who trespass in the Second Circle. Meet Bergil back at the Old Guest-house, where he stays.\n",
[843]="7005F869\n1\tTalk to Spall at Watchers' Roost\tSpall can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. Hermáth Stormhammer has permitted Spall to conduct a survey of Gloomingtarn on the condition that you accompany him. You should talk to Spall.\n2\tTalk to Vithin and assist the expedition in Glittengrof\030Talk to Lokur and assist the expedition in Ormgren\030Aid Spall with 'Surveying Glittengrof'\030Aid Spall with 'Surveying Ormgren'\tVithin and Lokur can be found in Glittengrof and Ormgren, respectively. Spall can be found at your side. Hermáth Stormhammer has permitted Spall to conduct a survey of Gloomingtarn on the condition that you accompany him and also aid the expeditions in Glittengrof and Ormgren. You should aid Spall with his survey and receive reports from Lokur and Vithin, two warriors of Hermáth Stormhammer's expedition. NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.\n3\tTalk to Spall\tSpall can be found at your side in Gloomingtarn. You have helped Spall complete his survey of Glittengrof and Ormgren. You should talk to Spall. NOTE: If you become separated from Spall, use the horn he gave you to call him to your side.\n4\tTalk to Hermáth Stormhammer at Watchers' Roost\tHermáth Stormhammer can be found at Watchers' Roost in Gloomingtarn. You have assisted Lokur and Vithin with their expeditions into Glittengrof and Ormgren, and Spall has completed the first part of his survey of Gloomingtarn. You should return to Watchers' Roost and talk to Hermáth Stormhammer.\n",
[844]="7005B22B\n1\tTalk to Múta outside of Gazat-fark\tMúta can be found outside Gazat-fark, located on the lowest level of Deepscrave and to the south-east of Aslíf.\n2\tFour dwarf smiths are being held at Gazat-fark. One has been spotted on the ground level, and the other on the second floor. The others may be trapped in Durbángh -- behind the doors on the second floor.\t\n3\tReturn to Náin in Aslíf\tYou have rescued the dwarf smiths. You should return to Náin in Aslíf on the upper tier.\n4\tTalk to Féli\tYou have returned to Aslíf and should talk to Féli.\n5\tTalk to Shúkurz\tYou should talk to Shúkurz and see what he has to say.\n",
[845]="700379F8\n1\tDefeat Half-orcs at Fushum Raus (total: 10)\tHalf-orcs can be found in their encampment south-east from the gates of Grimslade. You should defeat Half-orcs at Fushum Raus.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of Half-orcs near Grimslade, but there are too many to uproot the entire encampment. You have done all that you could here.\n",
[846]="7002F97D\n1\tTalk to Reeve Athelward at the Mead Hall of Cliving\tReeve Athelward resides in his Mead Hall at the east edge of Cliving. Ides has asked you to return to Cliving to thank her father for his support and so that she may continue on her training without your mentoring.\n2\tTalk to Thane Elfmar at the Mead Hall of Faldham\tThane Elfmar resides at the Mead Hall of Faldham, the southernmost town of the Norcrofts. Athelward wishes for you deliver a message: that Elfmar's Riders are to report to the city of Cliving for duty to the Reeve.\n",
[847]="70026E57\n1\tSend summons by craban (total: 6)\tThe crows can be found throughout the village of Lhan Tarren. You should send a summons to the each of the six farming and herding families of Trum Dreng.\n2\tTalk to the Elder in Lhan Tarren\tThe Elder is in Lhan Tarren, the Stag-clan village of Trum Dreng. You should speak with the Elder now that you have loosed the crows to deliver their summons to the distant farmers.\n",
[848]="70038600\n1\tTalk to Thane Mágla in Middlemead\tThane Mágla can be found in the Mead Hall of Middlemead in north-western Kingstead. Éowyn, acting as steward of Edoras, has asked you to aid in gathering the people of Middlemead in preparation for the journey to Dunharrow.\n",
[849]="7004E147\n1\tParticipate in Farmers Faire activities (total: 10)\tEvery day there is something to do for the Farmers Faire Festival. Come and join everyone in celebrating another lovely year and participate in the many Festival activities!\n2\tTalk to Campanula Chubb\tCampanula Chubb would like to thank you for your participation in the Farmers Faire Festival today.\n",
[850]="7002BFFF\n1\tTalk to Céola when you are ready to assault Lashkarg\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands. When you are ready to begin the attack on Lashkarg, you should speak with Céola. NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.\n2\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands. You should return to Céola with news of your victory.\n",
[851]="7002C625\n1\tTalk to Céola when you are ready to assault Lashkarg\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands. You should speak with Céola when you are ready to depart for Lashkarg. NOTE: This instance quest is meant to be run Solo and cannot be run in a group.\n2\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands. You should return to Céola with news of your victory at Lashkarg.\n",
[852]="70007D99\n1\tBring the lynx-hide to an Elven armoursmith to craft a cloak\tElves dwell in the hidden valley of Rivendell in the eastern reaches of the Trollshaws. Attacked by the Lynx of the High Moor, you bested the beast and discovered that your blow left nary a mark upon its hide. Having skilfully removed the hide, you should seek a light armoursmith that could fit the hide into a magnificent cloak.\n",
[853]="70062D7A\n1\tDestroy Orkish weapon caches (total: 10)\tMelia has asked you to destroy caches of Orc weapons in Tharbad. Tharbad is in southern Cardolan.\n2\tReturn to Melia\tYou should let Melia know that you have enacted her revenge upon the Orcs. Melia is at Stonecrop Encampment, north-east of Tharbad.\n",
[854]="7006EBC6\n1\tDefeat Ekhamâti soldiers (total: 12)\030Steal weapon caches (total: 8)\tYour mission is to steal weapons from within a nearby Ekhamâti camp and defeat as many soldiers as you can. You must make it out before reinforcements arrive.\n2\tEscape the camp before reinforcements arrive\tReturn to the entrance and escape the camp before reinforcements arrive! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tDefeat the Ekhamâti dôlo\tDefeat the Ekhamâti dôlo!\n",
[855]="7005AAF7\n1\tDefeat wandering fell spirits (total: 8)\tYou discovered fell spirits hidden in the forest near Mullach Cagar. You should find and defeat the wandering fell spirits.\n2\tTalk to Molkha in the valley\tYou found and defeated many fell spirits near Mullach Cagar. You should report this to Molkha in the valley.\n",
[856]="70066EE8\n1\tTalk to the supplier in south-west Tadrent\tA supplier sells goods in the south-west corner of Tadrent, in King's Gondor.\n2\tBring the shiny golden needle to Little Pip in Tadrent, King's Gondor\tLittle Pip is by the haystack in question near the northern entrance to Tadrent, in King's Gondor.\n3\tBring the shiny golden needle to Vexed Meldis in Tadrent, King's Gondor\tVexed Meldis stands by her home in western Tadrent, King's Gondor.\n4\tWait for her response\tVexed Meldis stands in shock.\n5\tTalk to Little Pip by the haystack in Tadrent, King's Gondor\tLittle Pip is by the northern entrance of Tadrent, in King's Gondor.\n",
[857]="7000B95A\n1\tBring improved toad stew to Indor\tIndor is at the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen. Wéthorm has returned the toad stew to you and asked you to give his compliments to Indor on its improvement.\n",
[858]="7002BFB0\n1\tDefeat insects (total: 8)\tInsects can be found at the nest, north-east of the Woodman camp in the Rushgore. Gisalic asked you to defeat many of the insects you discovered in the Rushgore.\n2\tTalk to Gisalic at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore\tGisalic is at the Woodman camp in the Rushgore, south-west of the insect-nest. You should return to Gisalic with news of your success.\n",
[859]="7000E5EE\n1\tFind Déornyd a new sword from a Gauradan\tGauredain roam to the north and west of Pynti-peldot, near the Lonesome Stones. Déornyd has asked you to replace his broken sword with one stolen from one of the Gauredain.\n2\tFind Déornyd a new sword from a Gauradan\tGauredain roam to the north and west of Pynti-peldot, near the Lonesome Stones. Déornyd has asked you to replace his broken sword with one stolen from one of the Gauredain.\n3\tBring the Gauradan-sword to Déornyd at Pynti-peldot\tDéornyd is at Pynti-peldot, south and east of where the Gauredain roam. You should bring the Gauradan-sword to Déornyd.\n",
[860]="7002CBE2\n1\tTalk to Idmar\tIdmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant. You should bring the symbol you found to Idmar.\n2\tTalk to Doron\tDoron is among his men on the crest of the hill in western Parth Celebrant. Idmar suggests that Doron might know something about the symbol you found.\n",
[861]="70007034\n1\tCollect hillborn woad (total: 4)\030Collect hillborn orchanet (total: 4)\tHillborn woad and hillborn orchanet grow on the hills of eastern Nan Amlug and Rhunenlad. Elúr has asked you to collect some hillborn woad and hillborn orchanet for Esteldín.\n2\tBring the dye-plants to Nethúr in Esteldín\tThe orchanet and woad you collected can be brought to Nethúr in Esteldín.\n",
[862]="70021595\n1\tBring the amulet-fragment to Mincham in the Lich Bluffs\tMincham is camped east of the road along the northern border of the Lich Bluffs. You should bring this amulet-fragment to the Ranger Mincham.\n",
[863]="7006F092\n1\tReach the mouth of the river\tTalmûri has asked for your help investigating claims of a poisoned water source in the area. Travel north-west to the mouth of the river to see if you can find any clues as to the cause of the tainted water.\n2\tInvestigate tracks (total: 2)\tYou arrived at the mouth of the river Talmûri told you about. Investigate the area and see if you can find any clues as to what may be causing the water to be poisoned.\n3\tYou arrived at the mouth of the river Talmûri told you about. Investigate the area and see if you can find any clues as to what may be causing the water to be poisoned.\t\n4\tSearch further up the river\tYou found tracks near the mouth of the river Talmûri told you about. They pointed further upstream. Follow the river to see if you can find any more indications of the poison's source.\n5\tInvestigate tracks (total: 3)\tYou found more tracks along the river. Investigate them to see what you can learn.\n6\tYou found more tracks along the river. Investigate them to see what you can learn.\t\n7\tContinue your search up the river\tYou found more tracks that point even further upstream. You have to be getting close now. Follow the river to find the source of the poison.\n8\tRemove animal carcasses (total: 2)\tYou discovered the source of the poisoned water to be rotting animal carcasses. Remove them to stop river's water from being tainted.\n9\tReturn to Talmûri in Burukíri\tReturn to Talmûri in Burukíri and let her know it wasn't Ekhamâti soldiers poisoning the river, it was only animal carcasses that began to rot in the water.\n",
[864]="7006C6E6\n1\tDefeat Ordâkhai warriors at Omboha ([see journal]/12)\030Defeat Dhómok Umûn\030Recover Raphuz's father's sword\tRaphûz directed you to an Ordâkhai camp north-east of Iridír. He believes that Dhómok Umûn, the warlord who stole his father's sword and arm, is there. In addition, you can help the people of Ambarûl by thinning out the Ordâkhai.\n2\tDeliver the sword to Raphûz at Iridír\tYou found Dhómok Umûn and defeated him, recovering Raphûz's father's sword. Return the sword to Raphûz at the settlement of Iridír.\n",
})
